From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/fb-helper: let fbcon soft-blank the console

On the Lumia the console runs on simpledrm, whose DPMS off cannot reach
the panel, so console blanking left the picture on screen. Add
drm_kms_helper.fbdev_soft_blank (default on): fb_blank() then reports
blanking as unsupported and fbcon clears the console to black and stops
drawing until it is unblanked (AMOLED pixels off).

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fb_helper.c	2025-07-28 02:56:38.000000000 +0530
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fb_helper.c	2026-11-15 09:59:34.877786090 +0530
@@ -53,6 +53,18 @@
 
 static int drm_fbdev_overalloc = CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_OVERALLOC;
 module_param(drm_fbdev_overalloc, int, 0444);
+
+/*
+ * Some fbdev devices sit on a firmware framebuffer (simpledrm) whose "DPMS
+ * off" cannot reach the panel, so a blanked console keeps showing its last
+ * picture. With soft_blank set, fb_blank() reports that blanking is not
+ * supported and fbcon falls back to its software blank: the console is
+ * cleared to black and not drawn again until it is unblanked.
+ */
+static bool drm_fbdev_soft_blank = true;
+module_param_named(fbdev_soft_blank, drm_fbdev_soft_blank, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(fbdev_soft_blank,
+		 "Let fbcon blank the console in software (black screen) instead of DPMS [default=true]");
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(drm_fbdev_overalloc,
 		 "Overallocation of the fbdev buffer (%) [default="
 		 __MODULE_STRING(CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_OVERALLOC) "]");
@@ -323,6 +335,9 @@
 	if (oops_in_progress)
 		return -EBUSY;
 
+	if (drm_fbdev_soft_blank)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	switch (blank) {
 	/* Display: On; HSync: On, VSync: On */
 	case FB_BLANK_UNBLANK:
